KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the generic category: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
no body for callee
--
libstdc++ defines generic_category() and system_category() in its
compiled library, and CBMC had no models: their "no body" checks failed.
Models are needed for std::print, which throws system_error when writing
fails (cpp23_probe_std_print).
